# BuildKit reads this (it sits next to the Dockerfile and takes
# precedence over a context-root .dockerignore). Paths are relative to
# the build context, which is the PARENT directory. We whitelist only
# the two repos the image needs so the rest of the workspace
# (lamheads-srv, lamheads-web, demo, …) never enters the build context.
*
!lmheads-python
!lmheads-codex

# …minus the heavy / irrelevant bits inside those two.
**/.git
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/*.egg-info
lmheads-codex/data
lmheads-codex/work
lmheads-codex/.lmheads-codex
